3.915 4.116 4.116 0 0 1 .46 1.839 3.255 3.255 0 0 1-5.524 2.3z" transform="translate(.5 .5)"></path> </g></svg> <span>Soil moisture</span> </a> <span class="arrow-up Soilmoisture"></span></div></div><div id="geophysical-measurement-content" class="modal-wrapper"><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Frozenground"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Frozenground" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7455" id="taxonomy-term-7455" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Frozen ground</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>When the temperature of the ground drops below 0° Celsius (32° Fahrenheit), it becomes frozen ground. Permafrost is a permanently frozen layer below Earth’s surface. It consists of soil, gravel, and sand, usually bound together by ice.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=frozen+ground" target="_blank">Explore Frozen Ground Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/frozen-ground-permafrost">Learn more about frozen ground</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-73614be66300c2584227c003024dd1a9b11751f4f6453f656b9192b54e77c65a"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/aquarius" hreflang="en">Aquarius</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/smap" hreflang="en">Soil Moisture Active Passive Data (SMAP)</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-643852cc5ac26e8b30e77909db8fa02787ea36d8d74c3b4929a088e5a02cafd5"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related research projects</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/18164"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-houses-QGreenlandFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=6ix3haey" alt="Houses in coastal Greenland" typeof="Image" title="Houses in coastal Greenland" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>QGreenland Project</div></a></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Glaciers"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Glaciers" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7450" id="taxonomy-term-7450" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Glaciers</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Glaciers are huge masses of ice, snow, rock, sediment, and often liquid water that originate on land and move down slope under the influence of their own weight and gravity. The two main types are continental glaciers (or ice sheets) and alpine glaciers.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=glaciers" target="_blank">Explore Glaciers Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/glaciers">Learn more about glaciers</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-286fde87f6a6c8a4ce4efd71d0dc9ddd560dd9f1d74ed38246731295782f1083"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/glims" hreflang="en">GLIMS: Global Land Ice Measurements from Space </a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/highmountainasia" hreflang="en">High Mountain Asia (HMA)</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat-2" hreflang="en">ICESat-2</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat" hreflang="en">ICESat/GLAS</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icebridge" hreflang="en">Operation IceBridge</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-052a6f4fb81d4f25755727b99249893bd2a2b105b4e8ee14bd7a8a881ac0133b"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related research projects</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/21545"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-ThwaitesFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=DF5uvGJ2" alt="Cavity Camp on the Eastern Thwaites Glacier Ice Shelf" typeof="Image" title="Cavity Camp on the Eastern Thwaites Glacier Ice Shelf" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>International Thwaites Glacier Collaboration</div></a></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Icesheets"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Icesheets" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7451" id="taxonomy-term-7451" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Ice sheets</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Ice sheets are masses of glacial land ice extending more than 50,000 square kilometers (20,000 square miles). There are only two ice sheets worldwide today, the Antarctic and Greenland ice sheets. They contain more than 99 percent of the land ice on Earth.</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=ice+sheets" target="_blank">Explore Ice Sheets Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/ice-sheets">Learn more about ice sheets</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-2d8340fe51be2b207fdfd2dbf32166ebd791c7030ec27af14cd2fcb081d2b27d"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/glims" hreflang="en">GLIMS: Global Land Ice Measurements from Space </a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat-2" hreflang="en">ICESat-2</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat" hreflang="en">ICESat/GLAS</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icebridge" hreflang="en">Operation IceBridge</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-184a5f5e9bfb1a6363d34e6c479bcaf665a22ee02836c4f66cb4a17a3ffecfcd"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related research projects</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/18164"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-houses-QGreenlandFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=6ix3haey" alt="Houses in coastal Greenland" typeof="Image" title="Houses in coastal Greenland" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>QGreenland Project</div></a></span></div></div><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/18163"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-ASINAFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=w3C3Jl0f" alt="Sea ice in Svalbard fjord" typeof="Image" title="Sea ice in Svalbard fjord" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>Sea Ice Today and Ice Sheets Today</div></a></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Iceshelves"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Iceshelves" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7453" id="taxonomy-term-7453" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Ice shelves</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>An ice shelf is a large floating platform of ice that forms where a glacier or ice sheet flows down to a coastline and onto the ocean surface. Ice shelves play an important role in slowing the flow of ice from glaciers or ice sheets into the ocean. When ice shelves collapse, research has shown that glaciers accelerate, flowing into the ocean and adding to sea level rise.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=ice+shelves" target="_blank">Explore Ice Shelves Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/ice-shelves">Learn more about ice shelves</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-4d84315145c3d629f6984c6f1bbb5ffb75cffe7f49f573d37107d57fdf250ec2"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/glims" hreflang="en">GLIMS: Global Land Ice Measurements from Space </a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat-2" hreflang="en">ICESat-2</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat" hreflang="en">ICESat/GLAS</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icebridge" hreflang="en">Operation IceBridge</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-9500c0eebe3f0d4188a76a30dc732fbf55a09ac33c4f4abc0b1fa157c6407fb6"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Seaice"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Seaice" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7452" id="taxonomy-term-7452" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Sea ice</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Sea ice is frozen seawater that floats on the surface of polar oceans and seas. It grows during each hemisphere’s winter; and it retreats in the summer, but does not completely disappear. The highly reflective white surface of sea ice reflects solar energy, cooling the planet. When it melts, the darker ocean absorbs more heat, reinforcing the cycle of melting sea ice.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=sea+ice" target="_blank">Explore Sea Ice Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/sea-ice">Learn more about sea ice</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-79e0e8dd5e9489aedd0316d045020fdf58e72888ff2c4f44096c727e8783469f"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsru" hreflang="en">AMSR Unified</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsre" hreflang="en">AMSR-E</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/aidjex" hreflang="en">Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment (AIDJEX)</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/ewg" hreflang="en">Environmental Working Group Arctic Atlases (EWG)</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat-2" hreflang="en">ICESat-2</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icesat" hreflang="en">ICESat/GLAS</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/modis" hreflang="en">MODIS</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-3"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/nimbus" hreflang="en">Nimbus Data Rescue Project</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icebridge" hreflang="en">Operation IceBridge</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/smmr_ssmi" hreflang="en">SMMR and SSM/I-SSMIS and AMSR2</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/viirs" hreflang="en">VIIRS</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-a897d78bc61bd1411ea3ba80a4a1db7645411d585b8f794f6d25842842400963"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related research projects</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/36495"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/photo-seaice-sipn-alia-khan.jpg.webp?itok=dVOtDMEA" alt="Sea ice in low-angled sunlight" typeof="Image" title="Sea ice in low-angled sunlight" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>Sea Ice Prediction Network (SIPN)</div></a></span></div></div><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/18163"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-ASINAFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=w3C3Jl0f" alt="Sea ice in Svalbard fjord" typeof="Image" title="Sea ice in Svalbard fjord" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>Sea Ice Today and Ice Sheets Today</div></a></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Snow"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Snow" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7449" id="taxonomy-term-7449" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Snow</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Snow is composed of frozen water crystals. It is not frozen rain, but a crystallization of ice that typically forms in clouds.&nbsp;Highly reflective, white snow bounces solar energy back into space instead of warming the planet. Mountain snowpacks also provide a slow release of fresh water into rivers and waterways.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=snow" target="_blank">Explore Snow Data</a></div></div></div><div class="cta-button-secondary field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="/learn/parts-cryosphere/snow">Learn more about snow</a></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-7113f167a71692c61669a49cb6782f65753978cdd5a184b0783b473058c681ef"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/aso" hreflang="en">Airborne Snow Observatory (ASO)</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsru" hreflang="en">AMSR Unified</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsre" hreflang="en">AMSR-E</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/aidjex" hreflang="en">Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment (AIDJEX)</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/clpx" hreflang="en">Cold Land Processes Field Experiment (CLPX)</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/ewg" hreflang="en">Environmental Working Group Arctic Atlases (EWG)</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/glims" hreflang="en">GLIMS: Global Land Ice Measurements from Space </a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/highmountainasia" hreflang="en">High Mountain Asia (HMA)</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-3"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/measures" hreflang="en">MEaSUREs</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/modis" hreflang="en">MODIS</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/snowex" hreflang="en">NASA SnowEx</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/icebridge" hreflang="en">Operation IceBridge</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-4"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/smmr_ssmi" hreflang="en">SMMR and SSM/I-SSMIS and AMSR2</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/viirs" hreflang="en">VIIRS</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-6492d846a8f4cca51d4dfeb370425fcc97251a5271c69c332f65b664a93ff5e2"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related research projects</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="col-md-4"><div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content"><a href="node/18161"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/small_story_image_style/public/images/landscape-RainONSnowFRPPPhoto.jpg.webp?itok=7PY59EK0" alt="Herding reindeer" typeof="Image" title="Herding reindeer" class="image-style-small-story-image-style" /><div>Arctic Rain On Snow Study Project</div></a></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="false" role="tabpanel" class="modal container" data-bs-backdrop="false" id="Soilmoisture"><div class="modal-content"><div class="modal-body container"><div class="close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" data-tab-close="Soilmoisture" aria-label="Close"><div class="close-container"><div class="leftright"></div><div class="rightleft"></div> <label class="close-label">close</label></div></div><div about="/taxonomy/term/7454" id="taxonomy-term-7454" class="taxonomy-term vocabulary-geophysical-measurement"><div class="content"><div ><div class="row custom-row-wrapper"><div class="col-sm-12 full-width"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-node-title field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><span>Soil moisture</span></div></div></div><div class="content-left"><div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-description field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Soil moisture is the water content of soil and is key to Earth's terrestrial water, carbon, and water cycles. It also influences how and when the soil may freeze or thaw, a key component of understanding frozen ground and its extent.</p></div></div><div class="content-right"><div class="field field--name-extra-field-explore-data field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="cta-button-primary"><a href="/data/search#keywords=soil+moisture" target="_blank">Explore Soil Moisture Data</a></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-collections field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-collections view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_collections view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-9b0d756b07311d95361469b2a1c23cf87694fda24eabe531eef3a8b775645f0a"><div class="view-header"><h3>Browse related data collections</h3></div><div class="view-content row"><div class="views-view-grid horizontal cols-4 clearfix col"><div class="views-row clearfix row-1"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsru" hreflang="en">AMSR Unified</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/amsre" hreflang="en">AMSR-E</a></div><div class="views-col col-3" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/aquarius" hreflang="en">Aquarius</a></div><div class="views-col col-4" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/clpx" hreflang="en">Cold Land Processes Field Experiment (CLPX)</a></div></div><div class="views-row clearfix row-2"><div class="views-col col-1" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/smmr_ssmi" hreflang="en">SMMR and SSM/I-SSMIS and AMSR2</a></div><div class="views-col col-2" style="width: 25%;"> <a href="/data/smap" hreflang="en">Soil Moisture Active Passive Data (SMAP)</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-extra-field-nsidc-geophysical-measurement-related-research field--type-extra-field field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="views-element-container"><div class="view view-geophysical-measurement-related-research-projects view-id-geophysical_measurement_related_research_projects view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-f8d33f85291707e2e31fbafb4802f08fc8d6fdd536abdd5e58585eafd757afdd"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="layout layout--onecol"><div class="layout__region layout__region--content"><div class="nsidc-block-type-content-list block-content-content_list block block-block-content block-block-content2255bb03-b540-41e6-8a94-e48b44eb8811"><h2>Featured news &amp; stories</h2><div class="nsidc-block-type-content-list block-content-content_list block block-block-content block-block-content2255bb03-b540-41e6-8a94-e48b44eb8811 list-content-items"><div class="content-items-list layout-items-carousel"><div class="list"><div class="col"> <article data-history-node-id="431952" about="/news-analyses/news-stories/navigating-new-ways-arctic-research" class="node node--type-article node--view-mode-carousel clearfix"><div class="node__content clearfix"><div class="field field--name-field-atrium-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div data-quickedit-entity-id="media/13879"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image-4 field--type-image field--label-visually_hidden"><div class="field__label visually-hidden">Image</div><div class="field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/carousel_desktop_image_type/public/images/atrium/gideonbillings-3.png.webp?itok=15-weza7 1x" media="screen and (min-width: 1200px)" type="image/webp" width="1166" height="415"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/carousel_desktop_image_type/public/images/atrium/gideonbillings-3.png.webp?itok=15-weza7 1x" media="screen and (min-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="1166" height="415"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/style